// Renode platform description for HDSC HC32F460 (Cortex-M4F).
//
// Renode upstream has no HC32F460 platform and no HDSC-specific
// peripheral models in renode-infrastructure (search:repo:renode/
// renode-infrastructure HC32 returns 0). Standalone with only what
// klipper HC32F460 firmware drives at boot:
//
//   - cpu (cortex-m4f) + nvic + dwt @ 168MHz (CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ for
//     the 168M clock-speed Kconfig option; the 200M variant runs
//     faster but timer_read_time only needs monotonically
//     increasing values from DWT->CYCCNT, not a precise frequency
//     match - the firmware's own SystemCoreClockUpdate reads
//     M4_SYSREG->CMU_CKSWR.CKSW which we leave as the storeback-
//     default 0, picking the HRC reset clock branch that bypasses
//     PLL setup entirely).
//   - flash (Memory.MappedMemory @ 0x0 size 0x40000) - HC32F460
//     has 256KB flash mapped at 0x0; klipper links the application
//     at CONFIG_FLASH_APPLICATION_ADDRESS (default 0x8000, with
//     0xC000 / 0x10000 alternates). All three application offsets
//     fit inside one 256KB region; no boot mirror is needed because
//     reset vector lives in flash directly (no SAM-style boot ROM
//     remapping).
//   - sram (Memory.MappedMemory @ 0x1FFF8000 size 0x8000) - 32KB
//     fast SRAM, the region klipper's CONFIG_RAM_START points at.
//     The chip also has a separate 160KB SRAM block at
//     0x20000000-0x20028000 but klipper links exclusively against
//     the fast SRAM (Kconfig RAM_START = 0x1fff8000).
//   - usart1: UART.HC32F460_USART @ sysbus 0x4001D000 with four
//     named GPIO outputs wired to nvic@0/1/2/3 to match the
//     hardcoded IrqRegistration mapping in src/hc32f460/serial.c
//     (RX -> Int000, ERR -> Int001, TXE -> Int002, TC -> Int003).
//     The HC32 INTC peripheral that performs the dynamic source ->
//     NVIC line remap on real silicon is left as a passive
//     storeback region in the launcher (see _EXTRA_PERIPHERAL_
//     STUBS_FOR_CHIP['hc32f460']); the firmware writes its source
//     IDs to INTC.SEL[N] but never reads them back, so the static
//     wiring above is observably equivalent for the only consumer
//     (serial.c). The .cs UART model is loaded into the runtime
//     via `i @hc32f460_uart.cs` emitted by renode_launcher before
//     LoadPlatformDescription runs - upstream Renode has no UART
//     model whose register layout matches the HDSC SR/DR/BRR/CR1/
//     CR2/CR3/PR ordering.
//
// klipper HC32F460 uses generic/armcm_timer.c (DWT + SysTick), so
// no chip-specific timer modeling is needed. PORT/PWC/MSTP/SYSREG/
// EFM/AOS/INTC writes go through Python.PythonPeripheral storeback
// stubs registered by renode_launcher (none of those regions
// busy-wait the firmware on a status bit - SystemInit just calls
// SystemCoreClockUpdate which is a passive read of CMU_CKSWR, and
// armcm_main only writes M4_PORT->PSPCR before entering
// sched_main).
//
// Configs covered: hc32f460-serial-PA3PA2 (anycubic-kobra-go-2022,
// anycubic-kobra-plus-2022) and hc32f460-serial-PA7PA8 (creality-
// ender2pro-hc32-2022). Both pin combinations use USART1; the
// PH2_PB10 / USART3 path is not yet covered (no in-scope printer
// config uses it).

cpu: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m4f"
    nvic: nvic

nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu@0
    systickFrequency: 168000000

dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 168000000

flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x0
    size: 0x40000

sram: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x1FFF8000
    size: 0x8000

usart1: UART.HC32F460_USART @ sysbus 0x4001D000
    RxIRQ -> nvic@0
    ErrorIRQ -> nvic@1
    TxEmptyIRQ -> nvic@2
    TxCompleteIRQ -> nvic@3
